  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The graph between two temperature scales <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is shown in the figure. Between upper fixed point and lower fixed point there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn></math> equal divisions of scale <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> divisions on scale <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>. The relationship for conversion between the two scales is given by :</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0033_d93b7c59f898.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 283px;\" />.</p>"
  },
